.Dd $Mdocdate: September 26 2026 $
.Dt FUGUORACLE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fuguoracle
.Nd blind PIN oracle service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the CGI program of the blind PIN oracle.
.Xr slowcgi 8
runs one process of it for each request, and
.Xr httpd 8
sends each request to
.Xr slowcgi 8 .
The program takes no argument and no option.
It reads no configuration file.
.Pp
The oracle holds one key share for each client.
It releases the share to a request that proves the correct PIN, and it
destroys the share after three wrong PINs.
It does not learn the PIN, and it does not learn the secret of the
client.
The wire behavior follows version 2 of the upstream
.Sy blind_pin_server
protocol.
.Pp
The program answers three endpoints:
.Bl -column "POST /set_pin" "a request envelope" "200, a response envelope"
.It Sy Request Ta Sy Body Ta Sy Answer
.It Li "GET /" Ta none Ta 200, an empty body
.It Li "POST /set_pin" Ta a request envelope Ta 200, a response envelope
.It Li "POST /get_pin" Ta a request envelope Ta 200, a response envelope
.El
.Pp
.Li GET /
is the liveness endpoint.
.Li POST /set_pin
stores a new key share for the client, and
.Li POST /get_pin
releases the stored share to the correct PIN.
.Pp
The body of a POST request is one JSON object.
The object holds one member with the name
.Li data ,
and the value of that member holds the base64 of the request envelope:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"data": "<base64>"}
.Ed
.Pp
The JSON reader is a small scanner, and the program uses no JSON
library.
The scanner accepts insignificant whitespace, and it ignores an
unknown member.
It rejects a second
.Li data
member, an escape sequence in the value, and each other shape.
The program reads exactly
.Ev CONTENT_LENGTH
bytes of the body, and it rejects a body above 4096 bytes.
It does not read the
.Ql Content-Type
header of the request.
.Pp
A 200 answer to a POST request carries the header
.Ql Content-Type: application/json ,
and a body of the shape above.
The value of the
.Li data
member then holds the base64 of the response envelope.
The liveness answer and each error answer carry an empty body.
.Pp
The table below holds the answer of each failure class:
.Bl -column "An envelope MAC or decrypt failure" "200, a junk key" "set_pin"
.It Sy Failure Ta Sy get_pin Ta Sy set_pin
.It "An unknown path or a wrong method" Ta 404 or 405 Ta 404 or 405
.It "A body above 4096 bytes" Ta 413 Ta 413
.It "Malformed JSON or bad base64" Ta 400 Ta 400
.It "An envelope length violation" Ta 400 Ta 400
.It "An envelope MAC or decrypt failure" Ta 500 Ta 500
.It "A payload extraction failure" Ta 500 Ta 500
.It "No entropy in the payload" Ta normal Ta 500
.It "A missing record" Ta 200, a junk key Ta normal
.It "A corrupt record" Ta 200, a junk key Ta 500
.It "A replay violation" Ta 200, a junk key Ta 500
.It "A wrong PIN" Ta 200, a junk key Ta not applicable
.It "An I/O or persist failure" Ta 500 Ta 500
.El
.Pp
The word normal in the table names a request that does not fail.
A
.Li get_pin
request ignores the entropy of its payload, and a
.Li set_pin
request creates a record that is absent.
The
.Li set_pin
endpoint proves no PIN, so a wrong PIN cannot reach it.
.Pp
A junk key is the answer of the junk path.
The program answers 200 with a valid response envelope, and the
payload of that envelope holds a fresh random key.
The status, the headers, and the envelope size are identical on each
junk path.
The client detects the junk key by the failure of its own decrypt
step, and the response bytes give no other signal.
The response time can differ between a junk path that writes and one
that does not, and the design accepts this difference.
.Pp
Each
.Li get_pin
request with a wrong PIN counts one strike, and a correct PIN sets the
count back to zero.
The third strike destroys the key share.
The program overwrites the record file in place with a dead record, it
calls
.Xr fsync 2 ,
and it removes the file.
The client cannot recover its secret through this service after the
wipe.
.Sh CLIENT PROVISIONING
The operator gives each client two values: the URL of the oracle, and
the static public key.
The URL is the public endpoint, for example https://oracle.example.org,
and it must not end with a slash: the client appends
.Pa /get_pin
and
.Pa /set_pin
to it.
The static public key is the hex string that
.Xr fuguoracle-keygen 8
prints.
.Pp
.Xr httpd 8
ends TLS, and the client does not require it: the envelope
authenticates the oracle, and TLS protects the metadata and the
availability.
A deployment with a private CA must also provision its TLS root
certificate, and the client verifies the endpoint with it.
.Pp
A client can hold a second URL of the oracle, for example an onion
address, and it selects between the two.
Both URLs must point at the same instance, because the records and the
static key live on one host.
.Sh BACKUP
The static key is the service.
A loss of
.Pa /var/www/fuguoracle/private.key ,
or of the
.Pa pins/
directory, makes the PIN unlock of every enrolled client permanently
inoperable.
The operator must back up the static key offline at enrollment time,
and must treat the
.Pa pins/
directory as precious.
.Pp
The operator must restore
.Pa pins/
only after an incident review: a restore rewinds the attempt counter
and the replay counter of each record to the backup time.
.Pp
A key rotation in place is not supported.
Every storage key derives from the static key, so a new key orphans
every record.
On a suspected key compromise, the operator must stop the service,
must generate a new key with
.Xr fuguoracle-keygen 8 ,
and must clear
.Pa pins/ .
The operator must then provision the new public key into every client,
and every client must run
.Li set_pin
again.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Xr httpd 8
and
.Xr slowcgi 8
set these variables, and
.Nm
reads them:
.Bl -tag -width CONTENT_LENGTH
.It Ev REQUEST_METHOD
The method of the request.
The accepted values are GET for the liveness endpoint and POST for the
two other endpoints.
A known path with another method answers 405.
.It Ev DOCUMENT_URI
The decoded path of the request.
It names the endpoint, and each other path answers 404.
.It Ev CONTENT_LENGTH
The length of the request body, in bytes.
It must be a decimal number of at most 4096.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
reads no other variable, and no variable holds a configuration value.
.Sh FILES
The two paths are compile-time constants, and each one is relative to
the
.Pa /var/www
chroot of
.Xr slowcgi 8 .
An operator cannot move a path without a new build.
.Bl -tag -width "/fuguoracle/private.key"
.It Pa /fuguoracle/private.key
The static key of the service, 32 raw bytes.
.Xr fuguoracle-keygen 8
makes this file.
.It Pa /fuguoracle/pins/
The record directory.
One flat file holds the record of one client.
Any caller can create a record, and the protocol sets no limit on the
count.
The operator must monitor the free space of the filesystem that holds
this directory.
The operator can mount a dedicated filesystem on
.Pa /var/www/fuguoracle ,
so that a fill cannot starve the rest of
.Pa /var/www .
.El
.Pp
A program outside the chroot reads the same two paths as
.Pa /var/www/fuguoracle/private.key
and
.Pa /var/www/fuguoracle/pins/ .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 after it writes an answer.
It exits 1 when a sandbox call fails, or when the write of the answer
fails.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Nm
logs with
.Xr syslog 3 ,
under the name fuguoracle and the facility LOG_DAEMON.
It writes one line at LOG_INFO for each request, and that line holds
the outcome class and the HTTP status:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
fuguoracle[28143]: ok_get 200
.Ed
.Pp
The outcome classes are:
.Bl -tag -width ok_live -compact
.It Li ok_live
The liveness answer of
.Li GET / .
.It Li ok_set
A
.Li set_pin
request stored a new key share.
.It Li ok_get
A
.Li get_pin
request released the stored key share.
.It Li junk
A
.Li get_pin
request took the junk path.
.It Li reject
The program refused the request.
An unknown path, a wrong method, a malformed body, a body above the
cap, and a short envelope each take this class.
.It Li error
The request failed inside the oracle, or an I/O call failed.
.El
.Pp
A third-strike wipe logs one line at LOG_WARNING.
Each I/O failure logs one line at LOG_ERR.
A failed read of the request body, a failed read of the key file and
a failed write of the answer log such a line.
The record store logs such a line for a failed read, a failed store,
a failed wipe and a failed lock.
No line holds key material, a payload, or a record name.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pledge 2 ,
.Xr unveil 2 ,
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Xr fuguoracle-keygen 8 ,
.Xr httpd 8 ,
.Xr slowcgi 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Dick Olsson Aq Mt hi@senzilla.io
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
The overwrite of a wiped record is a best effort against media
recovery.
FFS and SSD hardware give no overwrite guarantee, so the old blocks of
the record can stay readable on the disk.
The deletion guarantee of the wipe is weak for that reason.
The wiped record is also dead by its content: the key share of the
overwritten record is zero, and the file is gone.
.Pp
.Nm
sets the core limit to zero, and it applies
.Xr pledge 2
and
.Xr unveil 2
before it reads one request byte.
The promises after the unveil calls are
.Ql stdio rpath wpath cpath flock .
The program unveils the key file read-only, and the record directory
with the permissions
.Ql rwc .
.Pp
.Xr slowcgi 8
must run
.Nm
inside the
.Pa /var/www
chroot, as the user _fuguoracle.
The
.Xr httpd 8
workers then cannot read the key file.
